# EPI Generator

A Streamlit web application for generating Evidence of Property Insurance (EPI) from Excel data. This application allows users to:

1. Upload an Excel file containing insurance data
2. Select a producer and corresponding EPI template
3. Generate PDFs for each location in the SOV
4. Download all PDFs as a ZIP file

## Features

- Easy-to-use web interface
- Automatic template selection based on producer
- Support for custom template paths
- Progress tracking during PDF generation
- Downloadable ZIP file with all generated EPIs

## Requirements

- Python 3.7+
- See `requirements.txt` for all dependencies

## Installation and Local Setup

1. Clone this repository:
```
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/epi-generator.git
cd epi-generator
```

2. Install dependencies:
```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

3. Run the application locally:
```
streamlit run app.py
```

## Deployment on Render

1. Create a new web service in Render
2. Connect your GitHub repository
3. Set the following:
   - Build Command: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
   - Start Command: `streamlit run app.py`
   - Environment Variables: Add `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=true`

## Excel File Requirements

The application expects an Excel file with the following sheets:
- SOV (with header at row 11)
- Property Coverage Information
- Additional Remarks Page 1
- Additional Remarks Page 2
- Lenders

Required columns in the SOV sheet:
- Location Name
- Entity Name
- *Street Address
- *City
- *State Code
- *Zip
- *Real Property Value ($)
- BI/Rental Income ($)

Required columns in the Lenders sheet:
- Location Name (must match the SOV sheet)
- Lender Name
- Street Address
- Street Address 2 (optional)
- City
- State
- Zipcode
- Contract of Sale
- Lenders Loss Payable
- Loss Payee
- Mortgagee
- Other (Type in below)
- Lender Additional Information 1-12 (optional)

## Template Files

The PDF templates should be placed in the same directory as the application. The default template naming convention is:
- EPI Template - Garet Marr.pdf
- EPI Template - Jared Kahhan.pdf
- EPI Template - Matt Armstrong.pdf
- EPI Template - Matt Harrell.pdf
- EPI Template - Michael Shadeed.pdf
- EPI Template - Custom Format.pdf

## Customization

You can update the template paths in the `template_options` dictionary in `app.py` if your templates have different filenames or locations.

